itical. Without evidence, C is riskier.\n\nThus I think we should shift to Candidate B, acknowledging numeric memory gap but noting that we have no evidence of a problem, and that B's strengths are documented. We can also note that we have no evidence of C's reliability, which is a major concern. So we can change vote to B.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 and 3 both favor B, mention B's stress handling, conscientiousness, but also note crew cooperation concerns. We can argue that B's cooperation issues are less severe than C's unknown reliability and stress resilience, and that we can address via training.\n\nThus our public message: state we now recommend B, explain why, referencing facts: B handles stress well, very conscientious, good weather assessment, computer skills, but has pretentious, grumpy, uncooperative demeanor. However, C lacks evidence on stress resilience and reliability, making him riskier. Also note numeric memory unknown but not proven lacking. So we choose B.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
